1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:06,787
Microsoft already provides readiness assessments. But a findings report does not complete the work.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,971
Customers still need to know who acts next, what evidence is needed, and what remains blocked.

3
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:21,846
Meet AI Flight Deck: a guided follow-through workspace for Microsoft 365 pilots.

4
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:34,211
Start with Connect and scan tenant. Review Microsoft sign-in and permissions; other services can need separate connections.

5
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:44,859
Then select and approve your pilot people. This demonstration uses an isolated synthetic tenant.

6
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:52,323
Review thirteen domains. Technical checks, owner statements, and checks this version cannot perform remain distinct.

7
00:00:56,200 --> 00:01:01,229
Here, an identity baseline needs work. Choose the suggested next action.

8
00:01:01,433 --> 00:01:07,664
Record scope, owner and approval reference. Follow the administrator guidance outside Flight Deck.

9
00:01:07,867 --> 00:01:12,189
Report completion. Notice: the action is still not verified.

10
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:19,537
Consent to a fresh read-only collection. New policy evidence now verifies this supported identity check.

11
00:01:19,767 --> 00:01:28,323
For governance, record reviewed escalation contacts and references using simple fields. No JSON is required.

12
00:01:28,533 --> 00:01:34,896
The owner statement is accepted separately. It is not a technical check.

13
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:40,775
Download the pilot decision: supported checks, recorded owners, and what remains open.

14
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:47,679
An exclusion in later evidence reopens the identity action. Other requirements still block rollout.

15
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:53,751
AI Flight Deck: clear next steps, honest evidence, and no premature green light.
